  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read",
      "items": [
        "Links are containment (capability → feature), not calls. Each feature names its module and main file; click a node for the source.",
        "Stages 1-3 follow a warehouse project (README Features); change control, the AI assistant and collaboration cut across all of them.",
        "Stage 4, DW Implementation (dbt skeleton, SQL transforms), is announced as next phase in the README and has no code: not drawn."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What users get",
      "items": [
        "Analysts: understand an undocumented source (profiles, relationships, PII, AI descriptions) without hand exploration.",
        "Modelers: generated staging, AI-proposed Core/Mart, validated mappings linked to real columns, a quality score and approval gate, DDL out.",
        "Everyone: every change (human, AI, sync) arrives as a reviewable Change Set; lineage answers where a number comes from."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Uncertain",
      "items": [
        "Grouping into six capabilities is an editorial choice based on the README and module docstrings; modules do not declare it.",
        "Feature-to-file mapping names the main service file; some features span more files (api routers, internal/)."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
